{"ref":"BDB, בֻּנִּי","hw":"בֻּנִּי","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">בֻּנִּי</span></big>  <strong>n.pr.m. </strong><br><strong>1.</strong>  Levites, <strong>a.</strong>  <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 9:4\" href=\"/Nehemiah.9.4\">Ne 9:4</a>, but read perhaps <span dir=\"rtl\">בִּנּוּי</span> cf. BeRy & vid. <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 10:10\" href=\"/Nehemiah.10.10\">10:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 12:8\" href=\"/Nehemiah.12.8\">12:8</a> <a data-ref=\"Ezra 8:33\" href=\"/Ezra.8.33\">Ezr 8:33</a>; <strong>b.</strong>  <span dir=\"rtl\">בּוּנִּי (בֶּן)</span> <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 11:15\" href=\"/Nehemiah.11.15\">Ne 11:15</a>, but read perhaps <span dir=\"rtl\">מִן בְּנֵי</span> etc. cf. BeRy<br><strong>2.</strong>  a chief of people <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 10:16\" href=\"/Nehemiah.10.16\">Ne 10:16</a>, perhaps repetit. of <span dir=\"rtl\">בָּנִי</span> v <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 10:15\" href=\"/Nehemiah.10.15\">15</a> cf. BeRy.","next":"BDB, בִּנְיָה","prev":"BDB, בָּנִי"}